From ba3924b0eaeb77c046edc1597bd9856c573d2085 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: add lock-free RCU ChainAndMempoolSnapshot and O(1)
 getblocktemplate / submitminedheader
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add SnapshotPublisher RCU snapshots for lock-free read RPCs and O(1)
getblocktemplate / submitminedheader.

Coalesced prerequisite commits:

ecash/012 — avalanche: add mempool batch voting (avabatch) and preconsensus policy
Add Avalanche pre-consensus voting over frozen Merklix mempool overlay
batches (MSG_AVA_MEMPOOL_BATCH / avabatch).

ecash/013 — rpc: add Boost.Asio coroutine HTTP/RPC dispatcher and migrate long-polling
Replace the blocking HTTP work queue with a C++20 Boost.Asio coroutine
thread pool and non-blocking steady_timer long-poll waiters.


Build-prerequisite maintenance:
- Introduce the optional no-op CCoinsView prefetch hint API at its first call in 004; concrete overrides remain in 026.
- Place SHA-tagged-hash and reconciliation prerequisites beside their first overlay callers, and link the overlay foundation library. Original 005 and 006 are one compilation boundary.
- Supply storage and helper definitions at 007 for overlay queues, snapshot-defer scopes and the UTXO filter already called there; snapshot publication stays disabled until 014. This moves prerequisites out of 020/024; it does not remove forward call sites.
- Compile blocksnap.cpp with its first block-encoding callers in 009 instead of waiting for 020.
- Define the avabatch inventory ID required by the original 012 implementation/tests (0x20000006), preserve it in GetKind, and map its command name.
- Remove the stale treasury lock annotation until its V2 treasury mutex exists; no runtime treasury code is changed.
- Declare the existing mempool-batch vote variant and visitors with their 012 definitions; defer the V2-only supply gate until its V2 supply API is present.
- Compile the Merklix protocol handler at 010 alongside its first native tests rather than waiting for 020.
- Retain the existing per-tx SHORTTX validation path until the batch backend exists at 020. Reorder the PeerManager integration tests to 020, where the handler is installed; retain standalone wire/GF64 tests at the 010–011 boundary.
- Use the 011 header inventory constants as the single definition, and allow subsecond inbound scheduling intervals in NextInvToInbounds.
- Use the optional handler accessor for avabatch overlay registration until the concrete PeerManager handler member is installed in 020.
- Compile RCU snapshots and their already-used fee-controller dependency at 014; supply read-only mempool metadata accessors at their first caller.
- Provide a no-op backlog telemetry hint for the 014 snapshot caller; adaptive EMA tracking stays in 029.
- Reorder the V2 circulating-supply integration case to the V2 API introduction; it referenced absent SetV2BlockCirculatingSupplyForTest on L1.
- Reorder the batch-RPC case from the 014 RCU test file to 020, where its validation backend is linked.
- Compile the original Avalanche batch hashing helpers and define their avabatch wire command. Vendor/link BLAKE3 for the existing non-consensus batch-ID hash; L1 tagged hashes and block/transaction consensus hashes remain SHA-based.
- Correct the 014 snapshot-coalescing regression: keep removeForBlock mempool removals and prioritisation clearing inside one existing ScopedSnapshotDefer scope, as required by its native regression test. This is a behavioral repair, not a declaration-only fix.
- Correct the preconsensus test fixture to respond from the peer actually selected for each outstanding poll, rather than assume round-robin peer selection. Keep the original response content, policy/finalization assertions and round checks; fail explicitly if no matching poll exists.
- Repair missing MempoolBatch finalization dispatch: registerVotes removed finalized batch vote records but only dispatched block-index updates, leaving batches forever unfinalized and callbacks uncalled. Dispatch finalized batch updates to the existing finalizeMempoolBatch implementation and invalid updates to conflict tracking.
- Repair the Layer-1 preconsensus batch policy to compare the announced subtree against actual non-coinbase transactions, rather than demand that an 80-byte legacy header carry a V2 Merklix root. Align its positive fixture with the same legacy-header invariant; wrong-root and missing-transaction rejection assertions remain.

